iculty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104051/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104051"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104052/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "1c504b73-3714-5793-9249-3061d1a80938" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104052/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "e6b90e36-78c9-5372-b78d-bbacebb2dcc3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104052/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "9e46beea-3bba-5e34-99fc-b1ec80f604e6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104052/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "08a3fc23-0567-503a-baf2-f78b303817af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104052/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "28e5f4e2-ee74-578d-8b9f-93f1efb71068" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104052/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "505c801a-8430-5cf0-b998-0ff275882467" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104052/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-104052/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-104052/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-104052/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-104052/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-104052/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104052" :question/id #uuid "e9378234-bce1-51db-833b-fbd7d05969fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-104052" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/assets/8086893e4587e68f8257b75f2070cf622fa141199d6bd8960f7c4fd8e7bcb349.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $f(x)$ is **not** defined at $x=0$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)$ exists\n- $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph we can see that no value has been assigned to $f(x)$ at $x=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x) & =3, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function is not even defined at $x=0.$ The graph contains a break at $x=0.$ It's impossible to draw the graph of $f(x)$ without taking our pencil off of the paper." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104052/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104052"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
